<biblStruct xml:id="b46">
	<monogr>
		<title level="m" type="main">Marla&apos;s lease in Denver is for six months, which indicates that she does not have an open-ended intention to remain in Colorado indefinitely. (Misinterpretation -Omission of parts of the provided context while reasoning) -(Lease in Denver is for six months (A) -&gt; indicates that she does not have an open-ended intention to remain in Colorado indefinitely (B)) -Here B can not be true just because A is true, there are other factors which need to be true for B to be actually true</title>
